CITIML TO DATA CATALOG INTEGRATION – POC

1. REQUIREMENT

Rajat asked us to take three nodes from a CitiML
XPath, publish them to Data Catalog and create
parent-child relationships.


2. BASIC UNDERSTANDING

Dictionary : Container holding collections.
Concept    : Collection inside a dictionary.
Attribute  : Field inside a collection.
Node       : Individual element in CitiML XPath.
Symlink    : Relationship between metadata objects.
Lineage    : Connection between source and target.

MetaManager : UI to manage and verify metadata.
Swagger     : API documentation.
SoapUI      : Tool to execute REST API requests.
Data Catalog: Platform storing the metadata.


3. FLAT STRUCTURE VS HIERARCHY

Original CitiML hierarchy:

TradeNotification
    └── NotificationBundleDetails
          └── Events

Current flat Data Catalog structure:

CitiMLTest
    ├── TradeNotification
    ├── NotificationBundleDetails
    └── Events

All three collections exist at the same level.

To represent the original hierarchy, we create
parent-child relationships between their attributes.


4. OUR POC ENVIRONMENT

Environment: UAT2
Business: ISG
Provider: Olympus
Dictionary: CitiMLTest

SoapUI Endpoint:

https://qa.apac.isg.icgservices.citigroup.net

Common API prefix:

/isg/internal/data-highway

Query parameter:
env=PROD

Headers:
client_id: <approved client ID>
client_secret: <approved client secret>
Content-Type: application/json


5. STEP 1 – CREATE DICTIONARY AND NODES

API: Dictionary API

Method: POST

Resource:
/isg/internal/data-highway/dictionary-api/v1/ISG/Olympus/CitiMLTest

We created:

Dictionary: CitiMLTest

Concepts:
- CITIMLTRADENOTIFICATION
- CITIMLNOTIFICATIONBUNDLEDETAILS
- CITIMLEVENTS

Inside each concept, we created one String attribute
with the same name as the concept.

These are called self attributes.

Why?
Because our relationship API connects attributes.

Response:
{"version": 1}

Result: Dictionary created successfully.


6. STEP 2 – VERIFY DICTIONARY

API: Dictionary API

Method: GET

Resource:
/isg/internal/data-highway/dictionary-api/v1/ISG/Olympus/CitiMLTest/current

Result:
Verified all three concepts and attributes.


7. STEP 3 – GET LINEAGE REASON

API: System Info API

Method: GET

Resource:
/isg/internal/data-highway/system-info-api/v1/lineage-reason-type/all

Why?
The lineage creation request requires a reason.

We selected:

Reason: Other
Comment: CitiML XPath parent-child relationship POC

Reason ID:
33c1090f-9861-41cf-b43b-d51bfecf0d0b


8. STEP 4 – CREATE RELATIONSHIPS

API: Configuration API

Method: POST

Resource:
/isg/internal/data-highway/config-api/v1/attributes-symlinks/create

We created two relationships:

TradeNotification
        ↓
NotificationBundleDetails
        ↓
Events

Important request fields:

attributesFrom      : Parent attribute
attributesTo        : Child attribute
relation.type       : LINEAGE
relation.cardinality: ANY
transformationLogic : DIRECT
lineageReason       : Other
owner               : Approved SOEID

Initially, we received an error because
transformationLogic was missing.

After adding DIRECT transformation logic,
both relationships were created successfully.

We used LINEAGE to represent the XML hierarchy.
No actual transaction data was transferred.


